      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I have early check-in or late check-out at Nusa Lembongan accommodation?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Early check-in and late check-out can be arranged subject to availability. Standard check-in is 2pm and check-out is 10am. Most properties will hold your bags after check-out so you can continue enjoying the island."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do restaurants on Nusa Lembongan offer free pickup and drop-off?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Many restaurants on Nusa Lembongan offer a free pickup and drop-off service, which is especially useful for families and guests wanting to enjoy cocktails without worrying about transport."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the cancellation policy for Nusa Lembongan bookings?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "All payments are non-refundable as per The Lembongan Traveller's terms and conditions. Any cancellations due to illness, flight delays, or changes in plans should be claimed through your travel insurer. Travel insurance is strongly recommended at the time of booking."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Are there ATMs and money exchange facilities on Nusa Lembongan?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, there are money exchange outlets and ATMs on Nusa Lembongan. However, ATMs have withdrawal limits and can run out of cash. It is advisable to bring sufficient Indonesian Rupiah (IDR) cash from Bali before travelling to the island."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Will I get a refund on accommodation if my flight to Bali is delayed?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Refunds for flight delays are not provided by accommodation operators. You will need to claim compensation from your airline or travel insurer. The Lembongan Traveller team can assist with documentation required for the claim."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What happens if I get COVID-19 and cannot travel to Nusa Lembongan?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "If you test positive for COVID-19 and are unable to travel, you will need to lodge a claim with your travel insurer, as you would for any other illness or medical condition preventing travel."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What time is the last boat from Bali to Nusa Lembongan?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The last boat from Sanur, Bali to Nusa Lembongan departs at 5pm. If flying into Denpasar on the same day, ensure your flight lands before 3pm to allow enough time to reach Sanur harbour."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How do I get from the Nusa Lembongan harbour to my accommodation?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Boat companies provide complimentary transfers from Nusa Lembongan harbour to your accommodation on arrival. On departure day, the boat company will pick you up from your accommodation at a pre-confirmed time."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is there a doctor or medical clinic on Nusa Lembongan?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. East Medical Clinic in Mushroom Bay is a private practice open 24 hours a day, 7 days a week. You can reach them via WhatsApp at +62 813 3955 5515."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do I need a visa to visit Nusa Lembongan?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A Visa on Arrival is available for most nationalities and must be purchased at Ngurah Rai International Airport (Denpasar) before passing through immigration. Ensure your passport has at least 6 months validity from your date of entry into Indonesia."
          }
        }
      ]
