_wpb_post_custom_css:
a:link {
  color: #00a79d;
}

a:visited {
  color: #00a79d;
}
/* mouse over link */
a:hover {
  color: #6d6e70;
}
/* Hide mobile image on desktop */
.mobile-image {
    display: none;
}

/* Show mobile image and hide desktop image on smaller screens */
@media (max-width: 768px) {
    .desktop-image {
        display: none;
    }
    .mobile-image {
        display: block;
    }
}

faq_question_77897:
a:5:{i:0;a:2:{s:23:"saswp_faq_question_name";s:53:"Do beach clubs in Nusa Lembongan charge an entry fee?";s:25:"saswp_faq_question_answer";s:247:"Most do not. The majority work on a minimum spend for daybeds and loungers, which you put toward food and drinks, while many also offer free seating like beanbags and tables on a first come basis. A few rustic spots have no minimum spend at all.
";}i:1;a:2:{s:23:"saswp_faq_question_name";s:59:"Which is the best beach club for sunset in Nusa Lembongan? ";s:25:"saswp_faq_question_answer";s:216:"Ohana's on Jungutbatu is our top pick, with a nightly beach bonfire and live music. The pool at Suku Beach Club is great for panoramic sunset views, and The Pontoon by Lago is magical at golden hour out on the water.";}i:2;a:2:{s:23:"saswp_faq_question_name";s:57:"Are there family-friendly beach clubs in Nusa Lembongan? ";s:25:"saswp_faq_question_answer";s:172:"Yes. Sandy Bay Beach Club is the most family friendly, with a playground, a small children's pool and a kids' menu, plus a safe infinity pool away from the big ocean waves.";}i:3;a:2:{s:23:"saswp_faq_question_name";s:59:"What is the best beach club for swimming in Nusa Lembongan?";s:25:"saswp_faq_question_answer";s:182:"The Pontoon by Lago sits in calm, clear water and is one of the best places to swim on the island. For pool swimming, the pools at Suku Beach Club and Sandy Bay are both excellent.
";}i:4;a:2:{s:23:"saswp_faq_question_name";s:58:"Where are the best beach clubs in Nusa Lembongan located? ";s:25:"saswp_faq_question_answer";s:221:"Most cluster along the main beach of Jungutbatu, including Ohana's and The Beach Shack. Sandy Bay sits on the wilder west side near Devil's Tears, Suku Beach Club is on Nusa Ceningan, and The Pontoon floats just offshore.";}}
